# Intake

Pre-triage capture. Half-ideas, observations, irritations and things you
noticed in passing. No id, no file, no obligation beyond having written it
down. This is the cheapest layer in the lifecycle and it only works while it
stays cheap -- if writing a line here starts to feel like filing something,
the layer has failed.

An entry either matures into a task in `tasks/triage/` or gets struck out.
Sweep this file on a cadence you can actually keep; an intake list nobody
prunes is a list nobody reads.

## How an entry looks

```
  ## YYYY-MM-DD

  - **Short bolded subject** -- one sentence of context, so that future-you
    remembers why this was worth writing down at all.
```

Add today's date heading if there is not one already, newest at the top. The
two-space indent above is only there to keep the example out of the live
list.

